## 6. What We Need from AAAH Holding Corp

### 6.1 To Run the System (Needed at Go-Live)

| What We Need | Format | Why We Need It | When |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Project Schedule (Baseline)** | Primavera P6 or MS Project | To know what was planned, so we can measure how actual progress compares | Week 1 |
| **Work Breakdown Structure (WBS)** | P6 export or Excel | To link camera-detected milestones to the right activities in the schedule | Week 1 |
| **Site Zone Layout** | A drawing, sketch, or PDF of the site | To map which camera covers which area of the site | Week 2 |
| **Building Model (Optional)** | Revit or IFC file | Improves zone detection accuracy significantly | Week 2 |

### 6.2 To Train the AI (Important for Accuracy)

The AI comes pre-trained on general construction data. To make it accurate for AAAH's specific project types — whether high-rise, infrastructure, or mixed-use — it needs examples from your own past projects. The more you share, the more accurate the results.

| What We Need | Format | How Much | Why |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Past site photos** | JPG or PNG images from cameras or phones | At least 2,000 photos across your project types | Teaches the AI what different construction stages look like on your sites |
| **Milestone photos with notes** | Photos labelled with what stage they show (e.g. "columns done", "slab poured") | 500 or more labelled examples | Helps the AI understand what "complete" looks like for each activity |
| **Past completed project records** | Excel, P6, or PDF reports | 3–5 completed projects | Gives the AI a baseline for predicting delays and schedule performance |
| **Sample camera recordings** | Short video clips or recordings from site cameras | 2–4 hours per camera angle | Used to calibrate the AI to your camera angles and site conditions |
| **Zone boundaries** | A sketch or drawing overlay per site | One per site | Tells the AI which part of the site corresponds to which zone in the schedule |

### 6.3 System Access Needed

| What We Need | Details | Why |
|---|---|---|
| **Site Camera Access** | Video stream links (RTSP) or camera login credentials | So the AI can read the live feeds |
| **Project Schedule Access** | Read-only access to Primavera P6, MS Project, or scheduled exports | To keep the progress dashboard in sync with your schedule |
| **Company Login System** | Active Directory or single sign-on details | So all users can log in with their existing AAAH accounts |
| **Internal Network** | A fixed address on your network assigned to the server | So all users and cameras can reach the platform |

### 6.4 People We Will Need to Coordinate With

